    "medium_raw": "Wool knotted pile carpet, asymmetric knot.\nWARP: brown wool; Z2S; 16 threads per inch (65 per dm).\r\nWEFT: white wool; Z2S; 2 shoots after each row of knots; 12 knots per inch (50 per dm).\r\nPILE: wool; 7 colours: red, green (various shades, including brownish ones, throughout), light blue (apparently as a substitute for green), dark purple, pink, brown, white; asymmetrical knot open to the right and tied around 2 threads; 96 knots per sq. inch (1625 knots per sq. dm).\r\nSIDE FINISH: 2 cords overcast with dark pink wool.\r\nEND FINISH: Lower and Upper: some evidence of plain weave with red weft; loose warp fringe max. 9.5 cms. long\r\n",
    "classification": "Carpet",
    "styles": [
      "Turkoman",
      "Central Asian"
    ],
